            <ArticleTitle>A parlous state of storm and stress. The life and times of James B. Herrick.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>955-9</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>James B. Herrick saw medicine becoming more dependent on science but was unwilling to let the human values of the family doctor vanish. His philosophy was summarized in the phrase, &quot;The true physician must possess a dual personality, the scientific toward disease, the human and humane toward the patient.&quot;</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
